WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.100
I can't this is an expression that is
vilified in our minds beginning at a

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.670
young age every time a young child
announces this decision they are

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:13.799
corrected the first adult that hears it
asked them whether or not they have even

00:00:13.799 --> 00:00:18.090
tried generally this confrontation will
result in the child giving their task

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:22.500
another attempt until their attention
span moves on to something else the

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.130
adult will see this and chuckle to
themselves with knowledge that this is

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:31.769
just a child who is yet to learn the art
of art and virtue of perseverance by the

00:00:31.769 --> 00:00:35.790
time this child comes of age however
they will have been told by adults more

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:39.920
times than they could count that there
is no such thing as can't

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:44.850
it is interesting then to think about
how many adults seem to proclaim this

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:50.520
expression in their lives it is because
is it because like many things that

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:53.850
adults tell children they are simply
telling the child a general rule that

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:59.190
the child must follow but can be broken
once one has grown or is it because

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:03.090
these adults are simply repeating what
they were told as children without

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:10.619
thoroughly examining what the phrase I
can't truly suggests if you confronted

00:01:10.619 --> 00:01:14.520
an adult that claims they can't do
something with the same question about

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:19.619
whether or not they have tried the
answer will almost always be yes adults

00:01:19.619 --> 00:01:23.610
have learned enough to know that is
unreasonable to say they can't until

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:28.110
they have at least tried once therefore
the real question that we should be

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:35.070
asking in responses have you tried
everything have you exhausted every

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:42.479
possible option scenario combination
tool and approach I do not simply refer

00:01:42.479 --> 00:01:46.290
to the ones that you knew of at the time
you decided to undertake your task I

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:50.450
mean have you re also researched
possibilities that you had known about

00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:55.409
have you determined whether or not there
is another person out there that has

00:01:55.409 --> 00:01:59.780
performed the exact same task you are
attempting or at least something similar

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:05.189
have you exhausted this research have
you read every book blog journal

00:02:05.189 --> 00:02:11.910
magazine bathroom stall and website if
the answer to any of these questions is

00:02:11.910 --> 00:02:15.610
no then go back and try
because if you don't because you don't

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:21.400
truly know if you can do something until
you've tried absolutely everything the

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:26.680
fact of the matter is that rarely if
ever is the answer to all these

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:32.650
questions yes therefore what is it that
people actually mean when they say I

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:40.330
can't a more accurate but more verbose
way of saying it would be I don't care

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:47.320
about or want enough this task or the
resultant benefits of it in order to do

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:54.040
all that is necessary to achieve it I
was told countless numbers of times by

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:58.360
people during my month of marathons that
they couldn't run one marathon let alone

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:04.030
31 straight every now and then when I
had time I would discuss what they'd

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:09.760
said we would jointly conclude that if
something they cared about and depended

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:15.610
on them doing so it would be possible
the most common example I used was if

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:21.780
someone had a gun to your child's head
do you think you could do it then

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:27.310
therefore the phrase I can't denotes a
lack of investment as opposed to a lack

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:32.620
of potential or ability I do not mean to
say that every person I had this

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:37.090
conversation with should have had the
motivation to run marathons it was

00:03:37.090 --> 00:03:42.610
something that I decided to do not them
I merely wanted to express to them what

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:51.220
I am expressing here given the right
purpose and enough time you can what

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:58.050
happens if someone has said they can't
we have asked them if they've done

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:05.320
everything and the rare cases happen and
they honestly say yes do we concede that

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:10.870
then they can't nope if everything in
existence has been attempted enough to

00:04:10.870 --> 00:04:14.710
determine that it won't work then
congratulations you've been awarded the

00:04:14.710 --> 00:04:19.720
honor of being the person who must
invent the method or the tool or

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:24.430
determine the right combination whether
or not you will once again boils down to

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:29.290
how much you care
time they end up being that a person

00:04:29.290 --> 00:04:35.020
ends up trying for their entire life but
I suggest removing the phrase I can't

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:43.990
from your lexicon and replacing it with
I can't yet do this so that you don't

00:04:43.990 --> 00:04:50.700
risk being on your deathbed saying I
didn't

